Three simple graphs are given. For each, determine whether it has a
Hamiltonian circuit, or if not, a Hamiltonian path.

Graph $G_1$:
$V=\{a,b,c,d,e\}$, \;
$E=\{a\text{-}b,\;b\text{-}c,\;c\text{-}e,\;e\text{-}a,\;a\text{-}c,\;
b\text{-}e,\;e\text{-}d,\;d\text{-}a\}$

Graph $G_2$:
$V=\{a,b,c,d\}$, \;
$E=\{a\text{-}b,\;b\text{-}c,\;c\text{-}d,\;d\text{-}a,\;a\text{-}c\}$

Graph $G_3$:
$V=\{a,b,c,d,e,f,g\}$, \;
$E=\{a\text{-}b,\;b\text{-}c,\;c\text{-}d,\;d\text{-}e,\;e\text{-}f,\;
f\text{-}g,\;c\text{-}f\}$

