Section 5.7 Summary

{\small
| Type | Definition |
|---|---|
| Tree | Connected, no cycles, $n-1$ edges |
| Rooted tree | Tree with one root vertex |
| Binary tree | Rooted tree; each node has $\leq 2$ children |
| Full binary tree | Binary tree; each internal node has exactly 2 children; $\ell = i+1$ |
| BST | Binary tree with left $<$ node $<$ right at every node |
| Expression tree | Binary tree; leaves = operands, internal = operators |
}

Height = max level.\quad
Level/Depth of $v$ = edges from root to $v$.

